  This is a [1mbounded[0m change — one existing file, small addition — so I'll present a short design in chat rather than
  write a spec.

  One thing genuinely changes the shape of the code: [38;5;153m<main>[39m is currently empty, so there are no "items" to mark done
  yet. The fork is whether the checkbox is a one-off element or a reusable piece that renders per item.

  - [1mStandalone checkbox[0m — an [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m plus a label in [38;5;153m<main>[39m, a few lines of JS to reflect state.
    Cheapest; if you later want a list, the per-item wiring gets written then.
  - [1mReusable factory + seed items[0m — a small [38;5;153mcreateCheckbox(label)[39m function called for two or three placeholder tasks.
    Gives you the list shape now, but invents task data you didn't ask for.

  Everything here is cheap to change later either way — it's one file. I'd recommend the standalone version since you
  said nothing fancy, and I'd skip persistence (no localStorage) unless you want state to survive reload.
